Description: Make sway -C fail when an included file has errors
 sway -C logged the errors it found in files pulled in with include, but
 only errors in the main file changed the exit status, so a broken
 included file still passed the check. Regolith's sway configuration is
 almost entirely made of included partials, which made sway -C of little
 use for it. i3 -C fails in the same situation.
 .
 Errors in any file read while validating, the main one or an included
 one at any depth, now make sway -C exit with status 1. The errors are
 still reported with the included file's path and line number. Include
 patterns that match nothing, directories and unreadable files, and files
 already included stay non-fatal, as they are at run time. Starting
 sway, the reload command and its validation step behave as before.
Author: rego-port-bot <339843353+rego-port-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Bug: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/issues/6488
Forwarded: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/pull/9330
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
---
--- a/include/sway/config.h
+++ b/include/sway/config.h
@@ -545,6 +545,7 @@ struct sway_config {
 	bool reloading;
 	bool reading;
 	bool validating;
+	bool load_errors; // the main config or an included file had errors
 	bool auto_back_and_forth;
 	bool show_marks;
 	enum alignment title_align;
--- a/sway/config.c
+++ b/sway/config.c
@@ -438,6 +438,7 @@ static bool load_config(const char *path
 
 	if (!config_load_success) {
 		sway_log(SWAY_ERROR, "Error(s) loading config!");
+		config->load_errors = true;
 	}
 
 	return config->active || !config->validating || config_load_success;
@@ -509,6 +510,10 @@ bool load_main_config(const char *file,
 	set_from_resource_end_config_load();
 
 	if (validating) {
+		// sway -C fails on errors in included files as well
+		if (!is_active && config->load_errors) {
+			success = false;
+		}
 		free_config(config);
 		config = old_config;
 		return success;
